1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,800
Hello, my name is Adarsh Panicker, and welcome to SafeDash,

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,500
an ISO 26262 ASIL-D fail-safe digital instrument cluster

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:12,000
and telematics broker built on BlackBerry QNX Neutrino RTOS SDP 8.0.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,500
In modern vehicles, safety gauges and infotainment share a single multicore SoC.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,500
SafeDash proves Freedom from Interference,

6
00:00:20,500 --> 00:00:24,800
ensuring critical safety dials never freeze or drop below 60 frames per second.

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:29,500
With our drive mode selector, the cluster instantly shifts into SPORT Mode,

8
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:34,000
rendering an aggressive molten red cockpit glow and high RPM response.

9
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:40,500
Switching to ECO Mode activates an emerald efficiency theme, prioritizing regenerative energy recovery.

10
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:45,500
And in AUTOPILOT Mode, the interface transitions into an ambient autonomous HUD,

11
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,800
before smoothly returning to standard highway cruise.

12
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:52,000
SafeDash offers three dynamic cockpit perspectives.

13
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Here is our ADAS Focus panoramic layout, rendering ego-vehicle lighting projection and real-time millimeter-wave radar tracking.

14
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
For performance driving, TRACK Mode centers our 2D dynamic G-force accelerometer and lap telemetry.

15
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:10,500
Drivers can seamlessly return to the classic dual-gauge view at any time.

16
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:15,800
A single touch transforms the right tachometer into a modern EV Power Meter,

17
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:21,000
visualizing instantaneous traction delivery and green regenerative braking in kilowatts.

18
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,500
For DC fast-charging, SafeDash includes Battery Thermal Preconditioning,

19
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:31,000
actively ramping pack temperature to 32 degrees Celsius for optimal 350-kilowatt charging curves.

20
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,500
To meet upcoming Euro NCAP 2026 mandates, SafeDash monitors driver gaze and attention in real time.

21
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:44,500
We also calculate live road surface friction — from dry asphalt down to icy conditions — alongside a gyroscopic road pitch angle.

22
00:01:44,500 --> 00:01:53,500
Our side deck provides FMVSS 138 compliant 4-wheel tire pressure monitoring, tracking individual tire pressures and cavity temperatures.

23
00:01:53,500 --> 00:02:04,000
Next, our OBD-II and UDS Diagnostic Console captures freeze-frame telemetry snapshots for diagnostic trouble codes and supports Service $04 fault erasure.

24
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:09,500
Engineers can inspect live 11-bit CAN-FD traffic directly from the QNX driver layer.

25
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:15,000
Finally, our Safety Fault Lab injects full CPU starvation and subsystem crashes.

26
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
As you can see, the QNX Adaptive Partitioning Scheduler guarantees our 60% safety budget,

27
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,200
keeping the cluster butter-smooth with sub-20 millisecond watchdog recovery.

28
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:29,380
SafeDash is fully open-source and ready for automotive deployment. Thank you!
